# The fourth tooling step: the owner guard before a push, the comparison of
# paths by place, try's named jobs, the time profile, the pressure helper,
# the backends trap, scratch-test, the live headless entry and replace
# --text. Written with the code, and run with `cargo xtask mutate tooling-4`.

# --------------------------------------------------- the guard before a push

[break] the-terms-file-is-named-by-its-path
rule: A message about the terms file never spells out its path, which holds the home folder, a term.
file: xtask/src/owner_guard/local.rs
in: TermsFile::shown
find: Self::Default(_) | Self::Nowhere => DEFAULT_SHOWN.to_owned()
replace: Self::Default(path) => path.display().to_string(), Self::Nowhere => DEFAULT_SHOWN.to_owned()
caught-by:
    owner_guard::local::tests::a_file_that_is_there_and_cannot_be_used_refuses_the_push

[break] a-message-that-holds-a-term-is-printed
rule: Every line the local guard prints is held against the terms first.
file: xtask/src/owner_guard/local.rs
in: screened
find: Some(terms) if terms.matches(&text)
replace: Some(terms) if terms.matches(&text) && false
caught-by:
    owner_guard::local::tests::what_is_printed_never_holds_a_term
    owner_guard::local::tests::a_check_that_could_not_run_refuses_the_push_and_prints_no_term

[break] a-check-that-cannot-run-lets-the-push-go
rule: When the terms file is there and the check cannot run, the push is refused.
file: xtask/src/owner_guard/local.rs
in: verdict
find: Ok(checked) => checked,
replace: Ok(checked) => checked, Err(_) => (Vec::new(), 0),
caught-by:
    owner_guard::local::tests::a_check_that_could_not_run_refuses_the_push_and_prints_no_term

[break] an-unreadable-terms-file-is-taken-for-none
rule: A terms file that is there and cannot be read refuses the push; only a missing default file passes.
file: xtask/src/owner_guard/local.rs
in: load
find: && matches!(file, TermsFile::Default(_))
replace: || true
caught-by:
    owner_guard::local::tests::a_file_that_is_there_and_cannot_be_used_refuses_the_push
    owner_guard::local::tests::without_the_default_file_the_push_goes_on_and_a_named_file_must_be_there

[break] an-empty-terms-file-passes
rule: A terms file that holds no term refuses the push.
file: xtask/src/owner_guard/local.rs
in: load
find: if terms.is_empty() {
replace: if terms.is_empty() && false {
caught-by:
    owner_guard::local::tests::a_file_that_is_there_and_cannot_be_used_refuses_the_push

